// Character.fromString, which maxon's Character has not: a String of exactly one Character, which is one grapheme cluster
// (a base letter with its combining marks, a CR LF, an emoji sequence), read in place.
extension Character implements Parsable
	/// The Character the text is, when the text is one grapheme cluster and nothing else; an empty text, or one of several
	/// clusters, is `ParseError.invalidFormat`.
	public static function fromString(input String) returns Character throws ParseError
		let first = input.startIndex()
		let next = try input.indexAfter(first) otherwise throw ParseError.invalidFormat
		if next.bytePos() != input.byteLength() 'several'
			throw ParseError.invalidFormat
		end 'several'
		return input.charAt(first)
	end 'fromString'
end 'Character'
